a\n  - Aurora\n  - Lot 15\n  - Teja Residences\n\n30--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSime Darby Property | Integrated Annual Report 2021 (https://www.simedarbyproperty.com/annualreport2021/operations-review.html)\nciteturn307search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.8 years ago; Crawled: 2.3 years ago; New residential launches Elmina Green 5, City of Elmina; Lyra, Bandar Bukit Raja; Serenia Aiora, Serenia City; Dayana 1 & 2, Nilai Impian; and Maya Ara Residences, Ara Damansara — registered good take-up rates of more than 85%\nINTEGRATED ANNUAL REPORT 2021\n\n# Operations Review\n\nImageClick to switch between business segments\n\nDownload to read the full Operations Review\n\nDownload to read the full Operations Review\n\n  * ### PROPERTY DEVELOPMENT\n\nThe Property Development segment has approximately 15,400 acres of land bank, with a potential GDV of RM104.4 billion, located mainly in the Klang Valley, as well as in Negeri Sembilan and Johor. Our core offerings include landed-residential and high-rise products, as well as industrial-themed developments.\n\nKEY BUSINESS HIGHLIGHTS\n\nNew residential launches Elmina Green 5, City of Elmina; Lyra, Bandar Bukit Raja; Serenia Aiora, Serenia City; Dayana 1 & 2, Nilai Impian; and Maya Ara Residences, Ara Damansara — registered good take-up rates of more than 85%\n\nIndustrial and Entrepreneurship Park at the Pagoh Special Economic Zone with an estimated GDV of RM1.1 billion in the next five to seven years\n\n  * ### INVESTMENT & ASSET MANAGEMENT\n\nOur Investment & Asset Management segment manages the Group’s retail, office, and industrial assets in the Klang Valley, as well as in Singapore and the United Kingdom. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOur Distinctive Developments (https://www.simedarbyproperty.com/sites/default/files/2025-06/INTEGRATED-ANNUAL-REPORT-2024.pdf)\nciteturn307search16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; Right image shows high-rise integrated development towers with a pool and landscaping, captioned “Triara, Ara Damansara.” ...   - Maya Ara Residences\nOur Distinctive Developments\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\nTwo side-by-side development images under the heading “Our Distinctive Developments.” Left image shows a township housing scene at sunset with the caption “Laman Lakeside, Bandar Bukit Raja.” Right image shows high-rise integrated development towers with a pool and landscaping, captioned “Triara, Ara Damansara.”\n</visual_element>\n\nTOWNSHIP DEVELOPMENTS\n\n- City of Elmina, Shah Alam\n  - Denai Alam\n  - Elmina Business Park\n  - Elmina East\n  - Elmina West\n- Bukit Jelutong, Shah Alam\n- Bandar Bukit Raja, Klang\n- Serenia City, Sepang\n- Hamilton Nilai City, Nilai\n- Nilai Impian, Nilai\n- Bandar Ainsdale, Seremban\n- Bandar Universiti Pagoh, Muar\n- Taman Pasir Putih, Pasir Gudang\n\nINTEGRATED DEVELOPMENTS\n\n- Ara Damansara, Petaling Jaya\n  - Cantara Residences\n  - Maya Ara Residences\n  - TRIARA Residences\n- KL East, Kuala Lumpur\n  - East 57\n  - The Ridge\n  - The Rya\n  - The Veo\n- Melawati, Ampang Jaya\n  - Park One\n  - Melawati Corporate Centre\n  - Serini\n- Saujana Impian, Kajang\n- USJ Heights, Subang Jaya\n- Putra Heights, Subang Jaya\n  - The Serenade\n  - Serasi Residences\n  - Damayan Residences\n- SJ7, Subang Jaya\n  - Hype Residences\n- Subang Jaya City Centre (“SJCC”), Subang Jaya\n  - Aurora\n  - Lot 15\n  - Teja Residences\n\n30--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHow Gamuda Land Townships Are Built to Last: Mature Communities, Proven Track Record, and What That Means for Your Home | Gamuda Land (https://www.gamudaland.com.my/blog/how-gamuda-land-townships-are-built-to-last)\nciteturn307search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: last month; Set on undulating terrain, Jade Hills is a 338-acre township featuring a lush green landscape — the largest green park in Kajang. ... Alongside it, Eaton International School and the shops at Jade Square have grown into established fixtures that keep families rooted in the township.\n\n  * twentyfive7 Township Value and Lifestyle Guide\n  * twentyfive7 Buyer Guide: Family Living, Green Spaces & Community\n\nBandar Botanic\n\nImage: Gallery BB - 01.png\n\nPlanned around the “Home in a Garden” concept, Bandar Botanic is defined by its Central Lake and extensive parkland, which earned the Malaysia National Landscape Award.\n\nOver two decades, gated enclaves like Ambang Botanic have given the township a settled, secure character that keeps residents for the long term, while commercial hubs such as Botanic Capital and the neighbouring GM Klang Wholesale City keep daily needs within reach.\n\nToday, Bandar Botanic continues to evolve with modern lifestyle needs, from newer integrated commercial developments to upcoming rail access via the planned Bandar Botanik LRT3 station.\n\nJade Hills\n\nImage: Gallery JH - 04.png\n\nSet on undulating terrain, Jade Hills is a 338-acre township featuring a lush green landscape — the largest green park in Kajang.\n\nThe Jade Hills Resort Club has anchored community life since the township's early years, and Gamuda Land has kept it current, upgrading its facilities and adding to the residents-only clubhouse over time.\n\nAlongside it, Eaton International School and the shops at Jade Square have grown into established fixtures that keep families rooted in the township.\n\nValencia\n\nImage: Gallery Valencia - 01.png\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSime Darby Property Gears Up for the Next Release of Exclusive Condominiums with The Serenade | Sime Darby Property (https://www.simedarbyproperty.com/press-releases/sime-darby-property-gears-next-release-exclusive-condominiums-serenade)\nciteturn307search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.6 years ago; Crawled: last month;   * Follows the overwhelming success of the Company’s recent high-rise launches of Jendela Residences and Maya Ara Residences.\n\n< NEWS\n\nSime Darby Property Gears Up for the Next Release of Exclusive Condominiums with The Serenade\n\n  * The final phase of low-density condominiums at The Glades, Putra Heights;\n  * Follows the overwhelming success of the Company’s recent high-rise launches of Jendela Residences and Maya Ara Residences.\n\nARA DAMANSARA, 17 MARCH 2022 – Nestled within the self-contained township of Putra Heights in Subang Jaya, The Glades by Sime Darby Property Berhad (“Sime Darby Property or “Company”) is a 56-acre development with unique environment of peace and tranquility. Master planned with a low density of only eight units per acre, the freehold, gated-and-guarded enclave has excellent connectivity and accessibility to commercial hotspots, hospitals, international schools, and public transportation hubs.\n\nA desirable location and sound masterplan are just some of the reasons why The Alcove, The Glades’ first condominium development, achieved 100% take up for all 72 units during the recent pandemic. Jendela Residences at KLGCC Resort saw 80% take-up for its first phase upon launch, while Maya Ara Residences in Ara Damansara saw an incredible 90% take up on the day of launch. With limited units available, as well as being The Glades’ final condominium offering, The Serenade could well be the last chance for lifestyle upgraders to live in this exclusive community at a relatively affordable price point.\n\nImage\n\nThe Glades by Sime Darby Property is a 56-acre development with unique environment of peace and tranquility.\n\nThe Serenade is now open for registration at https://www.simedarbyproperty.com/putra-heights/the-serenade. Those interested can also book a private appointment to experience the tranquillity of The Glades and view The Serenade show unit at the Putra Heights Sales Gallery, open from 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. daily.\n\n-END OF PRESS RELEASE-\n\nAbout Sime Darby Property B